=== day
n: 9
title: The show page
subtitle: Views, details and My List
hours: 3 hours
page: index.html
slot: js | js | app.js
file: app.js = js
refs: @page, helpers.js

--- intro
Today ShowShelf gets a page for every show, with its cast and seasons, and a page for My List.

Instead of separate HTML files, the page now has three **views**: three `<section>` elements, of which only one shows at a time. Open the **index.html (whole page)** tab to see them: `#home-view`, `#show-view` and `#mylist-view`. Switching views is one more thing in the state.

Your code box starts with the finished app from Day 8, tidied into sections. The element lookups for the new parts of the page are already at the top (look for **Day 9**), so you can focus on what they do. Today's new code goes at the very bottom, under the line that says *new on Day 9*.

**This is your finished app.** On Day 11 it becomes your own website, online. Take your time, and read the code you add as well as writing it.

--- template
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>ShowShelf</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css">
</head>
<body>
  <header class="site-header">
    <div class="container header-inner">
      <a href="index.html" class="logo" id="logo">ShowShelf</a>
      <nav class="nav">
        <a href="index.html" id="nav-home">Home</a>
        <a href="index.html" id="nav-mylist">My List <span class="list-count" id="list-count">0</span></a>
      </nav>
    </div>
  </header>

  <main class="container">
    <!-- View 1: home, with the search and the grid of shows -->
    <section id="home-view">
      <div class="hero">
        <h1>What are we watching tonight?</h1>
        <p>Search real shows from TVmaze and keep your watchlist.</p>
        <form class="search" id="search-form">
          <input type="search" id="search" placeholder="Search shows, e.g. office" aria-label="Search shows">
          <button type="submit">Search</button>
        </form>
      </div>
      <div class="toolbar">
        <div class="genres" id="genres"></div>
      </div>
      <p class="status" id="status" hidden></p>
      <p class="status" id="empty-message" hidden>No shows match your search.</p>
      <div class="grid" id="grid"></div>
    </section>

    <!-- View 2: one show -->
    <section id="show-view" hidden>
      <p class="back-link"><button type="button" class="button-secondary" id="back-button">← Back to shows</button></p>
      <p class="status" id="show-status" hidden></p>
      <article class="show" id="show-details">
        <div class="show-header">
          <img class="poster" id="show-poster" src="poster.svg" alt="">
          <div>
            <h1 id="show-name"></h1>
            <p class="meta" id="show-meta"></p>
            <p class="rating" id="show-rating"></p>
            <p id="show-genres"></p>
            <p class="intro" id="show-summary"></p>
            <p class="show-links"><button type="button" id="show-list-button">+ Add to My List</button></p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <section>
          <h2>Cast</h2>
          <ul id="show-cast"></ul>
        </section>
        <section>
          <h2>Seasons</h2>
          <table class="seasons">
            <thead>
              <tr><th>Season</th><th>Episodes</th><th>Year</th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody id="show-seasons"></tbody>
          </table>
        </section>
      </article>
    </section>

    <!-- View 3: My List -->
    <section id="mylist-view" hidden>
      <div class="hero">
        <h1>My List</h1>
        <p>The shows you saved. They stay here after a reload.</p>
      </div>
      <p class="status" id="mylist-empty">Your list is empty. Press + on a show to add it.</p>
      <div class="grid" id="mylist-grid"></div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer class="site-footer">
    <p>ShowShelf · Web Dev in 11 Days</p>
  </footer>

  <script src="helpers.js"></script>
  <script src="app.js"></script>
</body>
</html>

