=== step seasons
title: The seasons table
minutes: 15
slot: js
--- explain
Each season becomes a row of the table: a `<tr>` with three `<td>` cells. Creating a cell takes three lines, and there are three cells per row. That's a sign you need a small function:

```js
function createCell(text) {
  const cell = document.createElement("td");
  cell.textContent = text;
  return cell;
}
```

`createCell` is ready below your code, and `row.append` can take several cells at once:

```js
row.append(createCell("Mon"), createCell("Rain"), createCell("12°"));
```

For the year, the season has `premiereDate`, a date like "2019-06-21". `yearOf(date)` in helpers.js keeps only the year.

> Real TVmaze data can have `null` for a season that hasn't been planned yet. `textContent = null` shows an empty cell, so nothing breaks.
--- task
1. Fill in the TODO in `renderSeasons`: add three cells to the row, for the season number, the number of episodes (`episodeOrder`) and the year.
2. In `openShow`, under `renderCast(data.cast);`, add `renderSeasons(data.seasons);`.
--- starter-append
// One table cell (<td>) with some text
function createCell(text) {
  const cell = document.createElement("td");
  cell.textContent = text;
  return cell;
}

// The seasons as table rows: season number, episodes, year
function renderSeasons(seasons) {
  seasonsBody.replaceChildren();
  for (const season of seasons) {
    const row = document.createElement("tr");
    // TODO: add three cells to the row: season.number, season.episodeOrder,
    //       and the year, yearOf(season.premiereDate)
    seasonsBody.append(row);
  }
}
--- hint
One line: `row.append(...)` with three `createCell(...)` calls inside, separated by commas.
--- hint
```js
    row.append(
      createCell(season.number),
      createCell(season.episodeOrder),
      createCell(yearOf(season.premiereDate))
    );
```
--- solution-replace
  renderCast(data.cast);
=>
  renderCast(data.cast);
  renderSeasons(data.seasons);
--- solution-append
// One table cell (<td>) with some text
function createCell(text) {
  const cell = document.createElement("td");
  cell.textContent = text;
  return cell;
}

// The seasons as table rows: season number, episodes, year
function renderSeasons(seasons) {
  seasonsBody.replaceChildren();
  for (const season of seasons) {
    const row = document.createElement("tr");
    row.append(
      createCell(season.number),
      createCell(season.episodeOrder),
      createCell(yearOf(season.premiereDate))
    );
    seasonsBody.append(row);
  }
}
--- check
